WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to our video next steps for sellers who've enrolled a brand.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:05.444
You've

00:00:05.444 --> 00:00:08.556
enrolled your brand in Amazon brand registry.

00:00:08.556 --> 00:00:09.000
Congrats!

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.200
After brand registry

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.000
approves your enrollment, both your brand registry and seller central accounts will

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.368
be associated with your brand, and you'll be ready to enjoy additional selling

00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:25.000
benefits, added protections, and greater control over your product detail pages.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.800
As you begin to explore all the opportunities available, make sure you

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.000
also complete a few key steps in order.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.769
Your first step after enrollment with

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.000
brand registry should be listing your products.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.667
If you haven't already listed

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:45.273
your brand's products in the Amazon store, wait until after you've received

00:00:45.273 --> 00:00:48.000
confirmation that your enrollment is approved.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.778
After approval, you can list

00:00:50.778 --> 00:00:53.000
using our standard processes.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.529
You'll be able to use the brand name field to

00:00:56.529 --> 00:00:59.000
select or enter your registered brand name.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.471
If you enter your brand name

00:01:01.471 --> 00:01:06.000
manually, make sure it matches the name on your trademark exactly.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:06.727
This helps

00:01:06.727 --> 00:01:12.222
ensure that your products are associated with your brand and integrated into the

00:01:12.222 --> 00:01:15.000
tools reserved for enrolled brands.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.333
To get step-by-step instructions for the

00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:24.167
full listing process, see the series of modules in our list products course in

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.000
Seller University.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.316
If you previously listed products within your brand by

00:01:28.316 --> 00:01:33.385
entering an unregistered brand name in the brand name field, you should contact

00:01:33.385 --> 00:01:38.000
Seller Support after your enrollment in brand registry is approved.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:38.931
Tell them that

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:42.966
you want to sync your existing listings with your newly registered brand name

00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:49.000
and provide the name of your brand as it appears on your trademark as well as a

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.000
list of relevant ASINs.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000
You should do this even if the name in the brand name

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.000
field isn't changing so that your existing products can be associated with

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.000
your brand's registration.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
If you previously listed your brand's products

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.571
in the Amazon store by entering or selecting generic in the brand name

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:13.800
field, you should delete those listings and create new ones using your newly

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.000
registered brand name.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.200
We can't associate an existing listing with a

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:23.000
registered brand after generic has been used as a brand name value.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:23.700
After your

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.250
products are listed and associated with your brand, you can activate each brand

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.000
benefit for your selling account.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.000
You can find them all by hovering over the

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.538
Brands section of the main menu in Seller Central clicking build your brand

00:02:37.538 --> 00:02:41.000
and scrolling down to the bottom of the page.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.500
There's no exact order for

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.000
activating selling benefits.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.200
Some brands configure settings for the subscribe and

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:54.000
save program then use brand analytics dashboards to understand the impact.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.182
Others review brand analytics dashboards first then decide to group and sell

00:03:00.182 --> 00:03:02.000
their products as virtual bundles.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.625
But it's important to note that some

00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:08.000
benefits are designed to be activated ahead of others.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.882
For example, a brand

00:03:09.882 --> 00:03:16.000
needs to create a store before they can use posts to attract followers.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:16.667
They also

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:20.889
need a store before they can create sponsored brands campaigns because those

00:03:20.889 --> 00:03:24.000
campaigns include a link to their store.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.118
In general, we recommend starting with

00:03:26.118 --> 00:03:31.800
selling benefits that can help grow the audience for your brand like A+ content

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.000
and stores.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:38.077
Then we recommend investing in programs like subscribe and save and

00:03:38.077 --> 00:03:43.091
virtual bundles which can generate repeat purchases and other types of

00:03:43.091 --> 00:03:44.000
customer loyalty.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.556
When you've optimized your brand's Amazon footprint and

00:03:47.556 --> 00:03:54.462
operations, we recommend informing your strategy with tools like Manage Your Experiments and brand

00:03:54.462 --> 00:03:55.000
analytics.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.462
It's also never a bad time to reinvest in

00:03:58.462 --> 00:04:00.000
protections for your brand.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.200
If you qualify for programs like Transparency or

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:09.053
Project Zero, enrolling in them can help keep you and your customers safe from

00:04:09.053 --> 00:04:12.000
counterfeits and other types of IP infringement.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.786
And every enrolled brand can

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:21.286
use the report a violation tool at any time to notify Amazon of suspected IP

00:04:21.286 --> 00:04:22.000
violations.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.643
As you use various brand benefits, you can also reach out to seller

00:04:26.643 --> 00:04:31.235
support if you ever suspect that one of your products hasn't been successfully

00:04:31.235 --> 00:04:33.000
associated with your enrolled brand.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.429
For example, if a product appears to be

00:04:36.429 --> 00:04:41.308
missing from a brand analytics dashboard, provide seller support with the exact

00:04:41.308 --> 00:04:46.000
brand name that appears on your trademark along with the ASIN that you

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.000
think may not yet be associated.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.273
Another step you may want to take after

00:04:51.273 --> 00:04:56.182
enrolling your brand is connecting it to additional seller central or brand

00:04:56.182 --> 00:04:57.000
registry accounts.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.000
By doing so, you can provide additional Amazon sellers with

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.077
listing privileges for the brand, meaning they can create or suggest updates to

00:05:06.077 --> 00:05:08.000
your brand's product detail pages.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.727
These additional sellers are eligible to

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:13.000
activate brand selling benefits too.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.625
Through separate processes, you can also

00:05:15.625 --> 00:05:20.909
assign one or more roles to additional brand registry accounts, which gives

00:05:20.909 --> 00:05:25.000
them access to various permission settings and protection tools.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.833
For more

00:05:25.833 --> 00:05:30.000
information about associating additional seller central accounts with your brand,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.000
see our seller university video "Manage Selling Benefits for Your Brand" and to

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:41.500
learn more about affiliating additional brand registry accounts, see our video
 "

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.000
Manage Amazon Brand Registry Roles".

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.000
This concludes our training.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Thank you and

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.000
happy selling in the Amazon store.
